  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oregon federal contract obligations totaled $63M in FY2027 to date. Award activity in the state shows 712 awards with an average award size of $88.5K. Obligations fell 97.6% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a sharp reduction from prior years: FY22 was $1.9B, FY23 was $2.7B, FY24 was $2.6B, FY25 was $2.2B, and FY26 was $2.6B. The Department of Agriculture is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $24M. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligations totaled $19.8M, and the Department of Justice obligated $6.5M. METRO WEST AMBULANCE SERVICE, INC. is the top vendor with $4.1M, followed by BAHFED CORP at $3.9M and TEAMGOV, INC. at $3.5M. Support Activities for Forestry is the largest industry by obligations at $12.2M, Other Computer Related Services accounted for $4.8M, and Ophthalmic Goods Manufacturing accounted for $4M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
