        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in Oregon right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture is the biggest buyer, obligating $24M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $19.8M and the Department of Justice follows with $6.5M. The General Services Administration obligated $3.9M and the Department of the Interior obligated $2.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top vendors and industries receiving federal dollars in Oregon?",
        "body": "METRO WEST AMBULANCE SERVICE, INC. is the top vendor with $4.1M, followed by BAHFED CORP at $3.9M and TEAMGOV, INC. at $3.5M. Support Activities for Forestry is the largest industry by obligations at $12.2M, Other Computer Related Services accounted for $4.8M, and Ophthalmic Goods Manufacturing accounted for $4M."
      }
